TVLWeightedContainers::getContainerInEpoch()
├── given epoch system is not started
│   └── it should return container with data
├── given container does not exist
│   └── it should return empty container data with zero duration
├── given container exists but is not active
│   ├── when epoch has no TVL data
│   │   └── it should return container with minimum duration
│   └── when epoch has TVL data
│       └── it should return container with minimum duration (inactive containers don't participate in TVL calculations)
├── given container exists and is active
│   ├── when epoch has no TVL data for any containers
│   │   └── it should return container with minimum duration
│   ├── when epoch has TVL data only for this container
│   │   ├── when container TVL would cause growth
│   │   │   └── when container duration grows
│   │   │       └── it should return container with increased duration by its growth rate
│   │   └── when container TVL would cause decay
│   │       └── when container duration decays
│   │           └── it should return container with decreased duration by normal decay rate
│   └── when epoch has TVL data for multiple containers
│       ├── when this container has majority TVL share
│       │   └── it should return container with calculated duration based on high TVL share
│       └── when this container has equal TVL share with others
│           └── it should return container with calculated duration based on equal share
└── given container duration would exceed maximum
    └── it should cap duration at maximum value
